BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tales from creating a universal Linux package for Open OnDemand wi
 th snap - Jason C. Nucciarone [Ubuntu]
DTSTART;TZID=US/Mountain:20260312T100000
DTEND;TZID=US/Mountain:20260312T102500
DTSTAMP:20261020T211446Z
UID:pretalx-good-2026-YHLDNY@pretalx.com
DESCRIPTION:This talk goes through the history of the Open OnDemand snap\,
  a single package for running Open OnDemand on any Linux distribution.\n\n
 The talk covers four sections: \n\n1. The Good\; successes such as automat
 ic backup/restore.\n2. The Bad\; challenges like bundling Passenger\, HTTP
 D\, and NGINX together.\n3. The Ugly\; implementing ad-hoc workarounds lik
 e a custom portal generator and custom Lua packages for administering Open
  OnDemand inside the snap runtime.\n4. What’s Next?\n\nIn the “What’
 s Next?” section\, I'll present the Ubuntu HPC community's plans to inte
 grate the snap into [Charmed HPC](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/charmed
 -hpc/latest/) to be the default user frontend. I will highlight blockers\,
  struggles\, hopeful contributions to Open OnDemand\, and areas where we n
 eed community assistance.
LOCATION:Main Hall
URL:https://pretalx.com/good-2026/talk/YHLDNY/
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
